    "prompt": "Use the attached reference video strictly as an EMOTIONAL ACTING and CAMERA reference: copy its escalating emotional close-up rhythm — the trembling tear-streaked face, the answering close-up of the wounded protector's face, the slow intimate cutting that tightens with each beat — and the raw facial acting of a farewell between a grieving youth and a dying guardian. But completely replace its characters, wardrobe and setting with the ones described below, and follow the beat timing written below for the ending (tear falls, frame floods to white, childhood memory) instead of the reference's final departure. Nothing from the reference video's visual design may appear: no pink hair, no cyborg or machine parts, no glowing blue implants, no neon signs, no modern city skyline, no flying figures.\n\nOne continuous dramatic anime emotional sequence, intimate and painful, built on close-ups and a slow escalating rhythm — this is an acting scene, not an action scene.\n\nAKAZA GENKI — a handsome young oni man with wild crimson-red hair in a long flowing low ponytail, two curved black oni horns, pointed ears, sharp amber-gold eyes, a black stud earring, and a rawly expressive face — in this scene his fury collapses step by step into open grief. He wears a black kimono with a white under-collar and antique-gold cloud patterns on the sleeves and hem, a deep-red obi sash with red tassel cords, a black cord choker with a small gold pendant, white tabi socks and black geta sandals, and carries a sheathed katana with a dark-navy wrapped hilt — it stays sheathed and untouched for the entire scene.\n\nThe setting is a night shrine courtyard in fantasy Edo Japan, half in flames: burning braziers and a torched wooden gate throw amber firelight and drifting embers across stone flags. Two hulking oni soldiers in dark lacquered armor and horned helmets grip Genki's arms from either side, holding him back. A few paces ahead of him, a wounded grey-haired old samurai guardian in a torn grey haori kneels collapsed on the stones, one hand pressed to his side. This is pure fantasy Edo Japan: no modern objects, no machines, no technology of any kind anywhere. All enemies are supernatural yokai spirits.\n\n0–1.5s: tight profile shot — Genki thrashing violently between the two oni soldiers, hauling against their grip, screaming, embers streaking through the firelight between him and the fallen guardian. 1.5–3s: reverse shot over Genki's shoulder — the old guardian lifts his head with immense effort, meets Genki's eyes, and mouths a single word: run. 3–4.5s: an escalating ladder of cuts onto Genki's face, each one tighter than the last — the fury in his amber eyes flickers, his brow breaks, and rage collapses into grief. 4.5–6s: macro extreme close-up of the guardian's dimming amber eye, firelight guttering in it as it slowly loses focus — then a matching macro of Genki's eye, wet and shining, tiny gold flecks in the iris, the burning gate reflected upside down in his tear. 6–7s: the tear breaks free in extreme close-up and falls in slow motion, catching the firelight — as it falls the frame floods gently to pure white. 7–8s: on the pure white emptiness a soft memory fades in: Genki as a small child — the same crimson hair, tiny horn buds — sitting curled and crying, while the guardian, younger, kneels beside him and rests a hand gently on his head. Hold there.\n\nPremium glossy modern anime, hand-illustrated painterly-cel hybrid: crisp cel shading on clothing, soft painterly hair with hard crescent speculars, large sharp eyes with layered amber iris gradients and twin catchlights, rationed antique-gold accents, warm firelight against deep night shadows, cinematic 24fps motion, slow deliberate emotional pacing with held frames. Faces carry the scene: every micro-expression is drawn deliberately. No text, no watermark.",
